<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>MediaRescue Privacy Policy</title>

    <meta
        name="description"
        content="Privacy Policy for MediaRescue, an offline-first Android media and storage management application."
    >

    <style>
        :root {
            --bg: #f6f8fb;
            --card: #ffffff;
            --text: #172033;
            --muted: #667085;
            --primary: #2563eb;
            --primary-dark: #1d4ed8;
            --border: #e5e7eb;
            --success: #15803d;
        }

        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }

        body {
            font-family:
                -apple-system,
                BlinkMacSystemFont,
                "Segoe UI",
                Roboto,
                Helvetica,
                Arial,
                sans-serif;
            background: var(--bg);
            color: var(--text);
            line-height: 1.7;
        }

        a {
            color: var(--primary);
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        a:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        .hero {
            background: linear-gradient(
                135deg,
                #2563eb,
                #4f46e5
            );
            color: white;
            padding: 70px 20px;
            text-align: center;
        }

        .logo {
            width: 82px;
            height: 82px;
            margin: 0 auto 20px;
            border-radius: 22px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-size: 40px;
            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
        }

        .hero h1 {
            font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .hero p {
            max-width: 700px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            opacity: 0.9;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
        }

        .container {
            width: min(900px, calc(100% - 32px));
            margin: 40px auto;
        }

        .card {
            background: var(--card);
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 18px;
            padding: 32px;
            margin-bottom: 22px;
            box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
        }

        .updated {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-top: 20px;
            padding: 7px 13px;
            border-radius: 999px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        h2 {
            font-size: 1.45rem;
            margin-bottom: 14px;
        }

        h3 {
            font-size: 1.1rem;
            margin: 22px 0 8px;
        }

        p {
            margin-bottom: 14px;
        }

        ul {
            padding-left: 22px;
            margin-bottom: 14px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 8px;
        }

        .highlight {
            border-left: 4px solid var(--primary);
            background: #eff6ff;
            padding: 18px 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            margin: 18px 0;
        }

        .privacy-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            gap: 14px;
            margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .privacy-item {
            border: 1px solid var(--border);
            border-radius: 14px;
            padding: 18px;
        }

        .privacy-item strong {
            display: block;
            margin-bottom: 5px;
        }

        .yes {
            color: var(--success);
        }

        .no {
            color: #dc2626;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 35px 20px;
            color: var(--muted);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }

        @media (max-width: 650px) {
            .hero {
                padding: 55px 18px;
            }

            .card {
                padding: 23px;
            }

            .privacy-grid {
                grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<header class="hero">
    <div class="logo">📁</div>

    <h1>MediaRescue Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
        Your files stay on your device. MediaRescue is designed
        as an offline-first Android application for finding,
        browsing, previewing, and managing media and files.
    </p>

    <span class="updated">
        Effective date: August 22, 2026
    </span>
</header>

<main class="container">

    <section class="card">
        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>

        <p>
            This Privacy Policy explains how MediaRescue handles
            information when you use the application.
        </p>

        <p>
            MediaRescue is developed as an offline-first application.
            The application is designed to process files locally
            on your Android device.
        </p>

        <div class="highlight">
            <strong>Privacy at a glance</strong>
            <br>
            MediaRescue does not require an account and does not
            upload your personal files to a remote server.
        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>2. Information MediaRescue Accesses</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue requires access to storage so it can find,
            display, preview, search, and manage files stored on
            your device.
        </p>

        <h3>Files and Media</h3>

        <p>
            Depending on your Android version and the permissions
            you grant, MediaRescue can access files and media stored
            on accessible device storage.
        </p>

        <p>
            This includes files such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Images</li>
            <li>Videos</li>
            <li>Audio files</li>
            <li>PDF documents</li>
            <li>Other accessible files</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            MediaRescue uses this access to provide features such as
            storage scanning, file searching, gallery views,
            previews, browsing, and large-file identification.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>3. How Your Files Are Processed</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue processes accessible files locally on your
            Android device.
        </p>

        <p>
            The application does not need to upload your files to
            a cloud service to perform its core functions.
        </p>

        <div class="privacy-grid">

            <div class="privacy-item">
                <strong class="yes">✓ Local processing</strong>
                File scanning and media discovery happen on your device.
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-item">
                <strong class="yes">✓ Offline-first</strong>
                Core functionality does not require an internet connection.
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-item">
                <strong class="no">✕ No account required</strong>
                MediaRescue does not require you to create an account.
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-item">
                <strong class="no">✕ No cloud upload</strong>
                Your personal files are not uploaded to MediaRescue servers.
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>4. Information We Collect</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue does not intentionally collect personal
            information such as:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>Your name</li>
            <li>Your email address</li>
            <li>Your phone number</li>
            <li>Your contacts</li>
            <li>Your location</li>
            <li>Your photos or videos on a remote server</li>
            <li>Your personal documents</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            MediaRescue also does not require user registration
            or an account for its core functionality.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>5. Internet Access</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue is designed to provide its core functionality
            without requiring an internet connection.
        </p>

        <p>
            MediaRescue does not use your internet connection to
            upload your personal files to a MediaRescue server.
        </p>

        <p>
            If future versions introduce online functionality,
            this Privacy Policy will be updated before or alongside
            those changes where appropriate.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>6. Third-Party Services</h2>

        <p>
            The core MediaRescue application does not require
            third-party analytics, advertising, or user-tracking
            services to provide its primary functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
            MediaRescue is distributed through third-party platforms
            such as Google Play and F-Droid. Those platforms have
            their own privacy policies and data practices.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>7. Storage Permissions</h2>

        <p>
            Storage access is required because MediaRescue's primary
            purpose involves finding and managing files on your device.
        </p>

        <p>
            You remain in control of granting or denying storage
            access through Android's permission system.
        </p>

        <p>
            If you deny the required access, some MediaRescue
            features, such as scanning and browsing device storage,
            will not function.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>8. Data Security</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue is designed to reduce privacy risks by
            processing files locally instead of sending personal
            files to remote servers.
        </p>

        <p>
            You should still protect your Android device using
            appropriate device security measures such as a screen
            lock and system security updates.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue does not intentionally collect personal
            information from children or other users.
        </p>

        <p>
            Since MediaRescue does not require an account for its
            core functionality, the application does not ask users
            to submit personal profile information.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

        <p>
            This Privacy Policy may be updated when MediaRescue
            introduces new functionality, changes how information
            is handled, or when legal or platform requirements change.
        </p>

        <p>
            The latest version will always be published on this page.
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>11. Open Source</h2>

        <p>
            MediaRescue is an open-source project. You can inspect
            the application's source code through the project's
            GitHub repository.
        </p>

        <p>
            <a
                href="https://github.com/everythingfreee/MediaRescue"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
                View MediaRescue on GitHub →
            </a>
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>

        <p>
            If you have questions, concerns, or suggestions regarding
            this Privacy Policy or MediaRescue's privacy practices,
            please contact the developer through the project's
            GitHub repository.
        </p>

        <p>
            <a
                href="https://github.com/everythingfreee/MediaRescue/issues"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
                Contact / Report an Issue →
            </a>
        </p>
    </section>


    <section class="card">
        <h2>13. Summary</h2>

        <div class="highlight">
            <strong>MediaRescue is built with a privacy-first approach.</strong>
            <br><br>
            Your files are processed locally on your device.
            MediaRescue does not require an account, does not
            intentionally collect personal information, and does
            not upload your personal files to MediaRescue servers.
        </div>
    </section>

</main>


<footer>
    <p>
        © 2026 MediaRescue. All rights reserved.
    </p>

    <p>
        Privacy Policy for MediaRescue v1.0.0
    </p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
